Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Share desktop combat damage assignment policy with
 headless GUIs

Extract the defender eligibility and lethal-damage/order prerequisites from
VAssignCombatDamage into forge-gui CombatDamageAssignment. The desktop
dialog and OpenMana bridge now ask this one Forge policy, so clients need
only transport and validate its numeric bounds. Preserve Forge lethal damage,
deathtouch, free division and modern unordered blocker assignment.

Source: Card-Forge/forge ed0333fecb1fea0671b3e50cadc1da4f71db5798,
forge-gui-desktop VAssignCombatDamage. No TypeScript or bridge card rules.
The desktop source is patched for shared ownership; the browser build still
compiles only forge-core, forge-game, forge-ai and forge-gui.

Written for OpenMana on 2026-10-08 (Prompt 30).
